WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.603
The DNA will get you every time.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.171
It's how the suspect in the mid-November

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.573
stabbing deaths of four Idaho

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.141
students was finally tracked down

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.442
and arrested.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.210
That's what we learned

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.311
with the affidavit of probable

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.346
cause was unsealed in Idaho court

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.247
this week.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.316
Investigators had found a leather knife

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.618
sheath on the bed of one of the victims.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.919
They found a DNA sample

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.755
on the button of the sheath.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.390
This and the cell phone records

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.924
tracing his whereabouts capped

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:25.592
the many weeks

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.127
long investigation

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.429
that included narrowing down which white

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.563
Hyundai Elantra

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.264
had been captured

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:31.965
on videos

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.433
in the neighborhood of the house

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.402
where the killings took place.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.203
A Washington State University officer

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:37.804
then located

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.739
a 2015 white Hyundai Elantra

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:42.242
in an apartment complex parking lot.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:42.842
The owner's

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.310
driver's license, information

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.312
and photograph were consistent

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.614
with a surviving roommate's

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.816
description of the mass suspect's

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:52.052
height and build and bushy eyebrows.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.020
Additionally, five days

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:54.888
after the murders,

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.056
the suspect had obtained

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.324
a new license plate for his car.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.893
The car was located at the suspect's

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.394
family residence in Albright's

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.996
Mill, Pennsylvania.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.230
CNN has reported

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.799
he was under surveillance

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.667
and he was seen cleaning his car inside

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.335
and out using surgical gloves.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.205
And depositing trash in the wee hours

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.841
in a neighbor's garbage can.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.341
On December

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.077
27, Pennsylvania law enforcement

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.378
discovered that trash

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.813
and sent it to the Idaho State

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.681
Lab for DNA testing.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.782
The very next day,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.251
the lab was able to match a DNA profile

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.020
obtained from the trash

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.620
as all

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.388
but assured

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.690
as being from the biological father

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:31.791
to a person

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.927
whose DNA was found on the knife sheath

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.795
as the document states.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:40.700
At least 99.9998% of the male population

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.002
would be expected to be excluded

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.437
from the possibility

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.506
of being the suspect's biological father.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.442
Joining me now is Sissy Moore,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:49.843
head of

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.044
Genetic Genealogy

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.313
Services for Paraben Nano Labs

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.081
Law Enforcement Unit,

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.250
which is made more than 200 successful

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.619
identifications of violent criminals.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.188
She's not worked the Idaho case.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.090
She stars in the documentary series

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.625
The Genetic Detective,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.160
now streaming on ABC.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.062
And she is also

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:09.662
has worked

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.397
on all ten seasons of the PBS

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.099
television documentary series

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.601
Finding Your Roots

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.870
with Henry Louis Gates, JR.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.037
Thank you for being here.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.372
What does this mean?

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.642
Single source of male DNA,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.512
which I'm reading from the affidavit.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.981
It means there were no other DNA

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.282
detected on that.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.284
Meaning sometimes you can have a mixture.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.987
You can have multiple people's DNA.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.422
You want to have single source DNA,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.891
if at all possible,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.626
because that really just ties

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.895
that one person to that item.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.796
Now, it was likely that

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.565
this was touch DNA.

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.567
Certainly it's possible there was blood.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.802
They didn't tell us what type of DNA,

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.305
but most likely it was touch DNA.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.541
And that would typically be just

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.975
a few skin cells.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:56.709
This might have been

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.012
a very small amount of DNA,

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.580
but because of today's

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.515
technological advances,

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.883
we can detect even the

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.585
tiniest bit of DNA.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.022
How reliable is touch DNA

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.023
if it is skin

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.292
cells in comparison to, say, blood?

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.361
It's a great question.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.397
It is more transferable.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.364
So of course,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.400
you would like to have blood.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.670
You would like to have semen or saliva.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.038
And they might

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:25.438
you know,

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.739
they haven't shown all their cards.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.008
We don't know all that they have,

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.443
but touch DNA

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.844
now that we can use it

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.246
because of the sensitivity

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.480
of our equipment.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.281
It also means

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.217
you have to be more cautious

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:40.220
about using DNA as your only evidence.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.488
So it's a really positive thing

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.557
that they clearly have other evidence.

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:46.659
This is just one piece of it.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.294
We have seen

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:52.031
DNA touch, DNA transfer in other cases.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:52.765
Of course,

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.800
it's fairly rare,

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.968
but it is something that you

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.536
have to be aware of.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.604
And make sure

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:00.807
that there are other aspects of the case

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.642
also pointing at the same person.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:05.411
Good news.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.246
I guess

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:06.746
it's hard

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.747
to commit murder

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.516
without leaving something behind.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.584
That's right.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.653
Yeah. I've been saying this for weeks.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.422
That type of violent, intimate crime,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.491
it is virtually impossible

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.159
not to leave something behind.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.195
Even if you are a criminology

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.830
PhD student.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.798
So I am not at all surprised

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.767
they were able to find something.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.235
Even if he tried hard

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:32.238
not to leave something, you still would.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.840
And that is great news

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.807
because what it means

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:35.642
is that

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.076
anyone who perpetrates

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.212
this type of crime in the future

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:40.346
should be aware

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.015
that they will be identified.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.383
They will be caught.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.285
There really is no reason

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.654
that we should see a serial killer,

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.922
serial rapist moving forward.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.790
This guy, you know,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.825
potentially could have become a Ted Bundy

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.560
or even a Zodiac

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.663
not identified 50 years later,

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.732
but because of the DNA technology,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.501
the advances that we're seeing,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.870
both in investigative genetic genealogy

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:04.971
and the ability

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.140
to use tiny amounts of DNA,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.208
we can identify someone,

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.243
whether they are in the law

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.978
enforcement database or not.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.548
CC the cases that you have cracked

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:16.783
for which you have become

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.452
famous are the cases that necessitate

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.820
you putting together

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.256
with in connection with a private lab,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.425
a very complicated family

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.793
history, family tree

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.928
and tracing back cousins and generations.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.130
That doesn't seem to be

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.299
what took place here.

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:36.135
Well, I don't think we can reach that

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.370
conclusion yet.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.039
Investigative genetic genealogy is simply

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.208
a tip. It's a lead generator.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:45.011
It should never be used as evidence.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.813
Against a suspect.

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.481
And so it is proper

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.682
that it would have been left

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.085
out of the affidavit, in my opinion,

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.053
because it should not form

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.322
the basis of an arrest warrant.

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.257
And so even though they didn't

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.392
put it in there,

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.728
I don't think we can rule it out.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.563
We don't know whether it was

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.431
what initially identified him

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.766
as a person of interest.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.334
And then they looked more closely

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:08.668
at that

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.269
tip about the car,

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.438
or it could have gone the other way

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.840
where they identified him

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.075
through that tip about the car.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.910
And at the same time,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:18.811
they were working on

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.413
the genetic genealogy

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:22.081
and may have built his family

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.150
tree to see if it was consistent

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.651
with what they were seeing.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.687
I have done that in some cases,

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.455
if there are persons of interest.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:30.723
You can very quickly

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.793
rule them out or potentially not.

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.461
Be able to exclude them,

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.629
which is what would have happened

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:37.530
in this case.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.499
Maybe they could have connected him

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:42.268
to one or more of those matches,

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.504
maybe a second, third, fourth cousin

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.238
and said, look,

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:45.772
you know,

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:47.173
this is somebody

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:49.308
who is a strong person of interest.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:50.943
So I think there's still a lot

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:53.179
for us to learn on what happened here.

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:56.048
I do think it is highly likely

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:59.152
that an advanced private outside lab

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:02.021
was used, at least somehow in this case.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.489
You know, we've all been hearing

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:04.357
whispers of this.

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:05.892
There's been lots of leaks

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:06.759
that investigative

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.661
genetic genealogy was used.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.697
So I do think that they were trying to or

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.533
in the process of doing so.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.968
And you make a great point.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.537
They, of course, don't have to put

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:19.272
in this affidavit of probable cause.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.107
They the prosecutors, all that they have.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:21.641
See, Seymour.

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:22.642
That was tremendous.

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:23.843
I thank you, as always.

